# Nothing here is needed. The app calls /api on its own server:
#   - built:      aftershock serve answers /api and serves the app (http://localhost:8000)
#   - developing: npm run dev forwards /api to http://localhost:8000
#
# If your API runs somewhere else while developing, point the forwarding at it:
# AFTERSHOCK_API=http://localhost:9000      (read by vite.config.ts; set it in your shell)
#
# Only for an API on a different site entirely (it must allow this app's origin):
# VITE_API_URL=https://aftershock.example.com/api
#
# Where the footer's [Documentation] link goes, e.g. your repo's README on GitHub.
# Leave it out to use the API reference at /api/redoc.
# VITE_DOCS_URL=https://github.com/YOUR-GITHUB-USERNAME/aftershock#readme
